{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"bf3992de1241f0a2761c9efa58581cb6bd262938a2171a1c4830bff116299f2f","digest":{"component_or_area":"test infrastructure / repo fixture isolation","key_entities":["tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py","test_copy_repoints_sibling_origin_and_keeps_refs_isolated","test_fixture_bare_remote_leaves_no_detached_upkeep_behind_a_push","receive.autogc","gc.autoDetach","maintenance.autoDetach","git maintenance run --auto --quiet --detach","shutil.copytree","objects/maintenance.lock","_BARE_REMOTE_UPKEEP_PINS","_init_bare_remote","GIT_TRACE2_EVENT"],"problem_keywords":["flaky test","race condition","git maintenance","detached process","concurrent mutation"],"propositions":["Test race occurs because a bare repository's receive-pack spawns detached background git maintenance processes that outlive the push command, causing concurrent mutations to the object database while shutil.copytree walks the directory tree","Vanishing paths during copytree are not limited to objects/maintenance.lock but include entire loose-object fanout directories (objects/2c, objects/2d, etc.) being repacked concurrently","The fix removes the race condition structurally by pinning receive.autogc=false, gc.autoDetach=false, and maintenance.autoDetach=false on the fixture bare remote before any push","A new guard test asserts the absence of detached background upkeep by running the push under GIT_TRACE2_EVENT and verifying no git maintenance run child carries --detach, with a receive-pack positive control to prevent vacuous pass"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","time